title: A Congress of the Left Currents
subtitle: The agenda changes with the caucuses still inside the party.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_faction_congress_timer <= 0 and (internal_dissent >= 25 or faction_vetoes > 0 or party_unity <= 60 or primary_active = 1)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_faction_congress_timer = 5
card-image: img/poland/cards/faction-congress.webp

= A Congress of the Left Currents

The television shot will show one Left. Backstage, the active caucuses are
counting what they can still protect. [? if barons_active = 1 and barons_in_left = 1: **[+ barons_name +]** wants control of the organisation and nominations.?][? if spring_active = 1 and spring_in_left = 1: **[+ spring_name +]** wants equality policy and visible parity.?][? if progressives_active = 1 and progressives_in_left = 1: **[+ progressives_name +]** wants open selections and a rights timetable.?][? if razem_active = 1 and razem_in_left = 1: **[+ razem_name +]** wants written guarantees and caucus autonomy.?][? if pps_active = 1 and pps_in_left = 1: **[+ pps_name +]** wants a social floor and a place for its historic name.?][? if social_patriot_active = 1 and social_patriot_in_left = 1: **[+ social_patriot_name +]** wants ownership of the material and regional turn.?]

Lewica Pracy MPs attend with OPZZ and wider-union delegates as a policy and
workplace network, not as another member party entitled to a block vote.

There is no point pretending that a merged organisation still has every old
party in the room. The congress can reward the currents that actually exist,
or let the strongest organisation write the rules for everyone else.

- @common_calendar
- @machine_compromise
- @barons_statute
- @spring_mandate
- @labor_protocol
- @progressive_timetable
- @razem_autonomy
- @pps_floor
- @social_patriot_turn

@common_calendar
title: Buy agreement on a common calendar
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. A shared process, without pretending the caucuses want the same party.
choose-if: resources >= 1 and faction_vetoes <= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The organisers lack one resource, or multiple caucuses have already declared vetoes.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.party_unity += 6;
Q.barons_dissent -= 3;
Q.spring_dissent -= 3;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
Q.razem_dissent -= 3;
Q.public_trust -= 1;
Q.turnout_readiness += 2;
Q.primary_cross_faction_pact = 1;
Q.primary_rules_written = 1;
Q.news_headline = "The active Left caucuses sign one precarious calendar";
!}

The leaders agree on candidate selection, programme deadlines and a rule against
surprise press conferences. The calendar does not dissolve the caucuses; it
simply gives the ones still present a way to fight without breaking the list.

- #poland_card_finish

@machine_compromise
title: Let the old apparatus run the congress
subtitle: Cheap, orderly and conservative. Every active challenger gets a reason to remember it.
choose-if: barons_active = 1 and barons_in_left = 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no active SLD organisation to run the room.
on-arrival: resources += 1; barons_strength += 2; barons_dissent -= 5; local_network += 2; spring_dissent += 3 if spring_active = 1; labor_dissent += 2; union_trust -= 2; progressives_dissent += 5 if progressives_active = 1; razem_dissent += 5 if razem_active = 1; pps_dissent += 3 if pps_active = 1; social_patriot_dissent += 4 if social_patriot_active = 1; progressive_credibility -= 2; party_unity += 1; rural_support += 2; pensioner_support += 2; young_support -= 1; primary_machine_slate = 1; news_headline = "The organisational establishment produces a flawless congress"

The hall is full, the votes occur on time and every regional chair knows their
instructions. The alliance looks professional. It also looks more like the
organisation that inherited the party than the coalition it promised to become.

- #poland_card_finish

@barons_statute
title: Give the organisational establishment the regional statute
subtitle: SLD keeps its machine, but the other currents receive formal seats at the table.
choose-if: barons_active = 1 and barons_in_left = 1 and resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The organisational establishment is absent, or the congress lacks one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; barons_dissent -= 18; barons_strength += 2; local_network += 3; party_unity += 2; primary_rules_written = 1; spring_dissent += 2 if spring_active = 1; progressives_dissent += 2 if progressives_active = 1; razem_dissent += 2 if razem_active = 1; news_headline = "The organisational establishment signs a plural congress statute"

Regional offices keep their autonomy, but nominations and programme deadlines
must now pass through a mixed committee. The machine wins protection without
being allowed to call its own inheritance the whole party.

- #poland_card_finish

@spring_mandate
title: Hand equality policy to the [+ spring_name +] current
subtitle: The merged party keeps a Wiosna-derived mandate only while its current is still active.
choose-if: spring_active = 1 and spring_in_left = 1 and spring_strength + progressives_strength >= 25
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ spring_name +] current is no longer active, or lacks the weight to lead this mandate.
on-arrival: spring_strength += 2; spring_dissent -= 12; progressives_dissent -= 4 if progressives_active = 1; feminist_trust += 5; progressive_credibility += 4; media_capacity += 2; party_unity -= 1; women_led_mandate = 1; news_headline = "The active Wiosna current wins the equality mandate"

The delegates give the equality brief to the current that still carries
Wiosna's network and public profile. If that organisation has already merged
away, this demand never appears on the ballot.

- #poland_card_finish

@labor_protocol
title: Ratify the Lewica Pracy–union protocol
subtitle: Wages, public services and workplace access become an auditable cross-party commitment.
choose-if: labor_active = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Lewica Pracy's parliamentary and union network is not represented.
on-arrival: labor_dissent -= 12; labor_credibility += 5; union_trust += 8; opzz_cooperation += 8; labor_mobilization += 5; workers_support += 3; public_sector_support += 2; budget_promises += 1; razem_cooperation += 2; razem_dissent -= 2; progressives_dissent -= 1; spring_dissent -= 1; barons_dissent += 2; party_unity += 1; news_headline = "The congress ratifies a union-backed labour protocol"

Union and public-service organisers leave with dates, policy ownership and a
way to call a breach. It is less photogenic than a new slogan, but much harder
for any SLD, Razem, Wiosna or Wspólne Jutro leadership to quietly forget.

- #poland_card_finish

@progressive_timetable
title: Put the younger progressive current in charge of the rights timetable
subtitle: Open selections and a binding equality calendar; the apparatus loses room to improvise.
choose-if: progressives_active = 1 and progressives_in_left = 1 and progressives_strength >= 12
unavailable-subtitle: The younger progressive current is not active or cannot yet carry the timetable.
on-arrival: progressives_strength += 2; progressives_dissent -= 15; progressive_credibility += 5; feminist_trust += 4; movement_autonomy += 3; media_capacity += 1; barons_dissent += 4 if barons_active = 1; party_unity -= 1; women_led_mandate = 1; primary_new_generation = 1; news_headline = "The younger progressive current takes the rights timetable"

The congress grants the newer organisers real authority over selections and
equality policy. The photographs change, and so does the list of people who can
veto a retreat.

- #poland_card_finish

@razem_autonomy
title: Write Razem's autonomy guarantees into the statute
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Programme milestones and a caucus veto keep the movement inside.
choose-if: razem_active = 1 and razem_in_left = 1 and resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Razem is absent from the common club, or the guarantee cannot be funded.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; razem_dissent -= 18; razem_cooperation += 8; party_unity += 2; budget_promises += 1; barons_dissent += 3 if barons_active = 1; news_headline = "Razem turns programme guarantees into a congress statute"

Razem accepts the common list only after the promises acquire dates, owners and
an exit from any vote that breaks them. The movement has not been absorbed; it
has been given a reason to stay.

- #poland_card_finish

@pps_floor
title: Reserve a seat for the PPS social floor
subtitle: A small historic current gets a programme seat and labour legitimacy.
choose-if: pps_active = 1 and pps_in_left = 1
unavailable-subtitle: PPS is not an active current in this congress.
on-arrival: pps_strength += 1; pps_dissent -= 14; labor_credibility += 3; budget_promises += 1; party_unity += 1; news_headline = "The congress gives PPS a seat for the social floor"

The PPS circle is too small to run the hall, but large enough to make the
party's social promise sound less like borrowed language. Its name remains in
the coalition because it has been given work rather than ceremonial applause.

- #poland_card_finish

@social_patriot_turn
title: Let the social-patriot current own the material turn
subtitle: Regional development and welfare sovereignty gain an organiser instead of a slogan.
choose-if: social_patriot_active = 1 and social_patriot_in_left = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Lewica Patriotyczna has not yet become an active organisation.
on-arrival: social_patriot_strength += 2; social_patriot_dissent -= 15; social_patriot_local_organisation += 3; rural_support += 2; pensioner_support += 2; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "The social-patriot current claims the material agenda"

The regional organisers receive ownership of development, welfare referrals and
the party's answer to sovereignty politics. The common Left becomes broader,
but less able to pretend that every current speaks in one register.

- #poland_card_finish
